# Quotio — every one of these is optional.
#
# With an empty .env.local the whole product works: build, edit, publish,
# embed, capture leads, read analytics. Copy this file to .env.local only when
# you want to swap a piece out for the real thing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where this deployment lives. Used in hosted links and embed snippets, so it
# has to be right in production or copied snippets will point at localhost.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage. Default is a JSON file under .data/ — no setup, survives restarts,
# fine for development and a demo. Switch to Postgres when you have users.
#   1. run supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql in the Supabase SQL editor
#   2. set DATA_STORE=supabase and the two keys below
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA_STORE=supabase
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Widget generation. Without a key, prompts are parsed locally — it reads
# prices and questions out of the sentence and builds a working widget, and
# falls back to the closest template when it can't. With a key, the model does
# a much better job and the local parser becomes the safety net.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# AI_PROVIDER=heuristic     # force the local parser even with a key set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Billing. Plan limits are enforced with or without these; without them the
# pricing page says card payments aren't switched on rather than showing a
# checkout button that does nothing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# One price id per plan per billing period. A deployment can configure just
# the yearly pair, just the monthly pair, or all four — the pricing page and
# the upgrade buttons only offer the periods that have an id behind them.
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=
# STRIPE_PRICE_BUSINESS=
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY=
# STRIPE_PRICE_BUSINESS_MONTHLY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email. Without these the product still works — password reset falls back to
# telling people to write to support, rather than pretending a link is coming.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# EMAIL_FROM="MEKMI <hello@mekmi.app>"
# Only if your deployment sends through an egress proxy:
# RESEND_API_URL=https://api.resend.com/emails
